 "content": "Let's see if actually know sales. 1. Discovery questions. 2. Pain points. 3. Objection handling. 4. Value proposition. 5. Features vs. benefits. 6. Qualification. 7. Rapport. 8. Follow-up. 9. Closing. 10. Upselling. 11. Cross-selling. 12. Negotiation. 13. Urgency. 14. Social proof. 15. Anchoring. 16. Framing. 17. Active listening. 18. Buying signals. 19. Decision-maker identification. If you know all this and actively practicing, you are a master closer my man. [On-screen text: 19 Must Know Sales Concepts, 1. Discovery questions, 2. Pain points, 3. Objection handling, 4. Value proposition, 5. Features vs. benefits, 6. Qualification, 7. Rapport, 8. Follow-up, 9. Closing, 10. Upselling, 11. Cross-selling, 12. Negotiation, 13. Urgency, 14. Social proof, 15. Anchoring, 16. Framing, 17. Active listening, 18. Buying signals, 19. Decision-maker identification, Comment \"sales\" and I will send you the guide explaining each of the terms and how you can easily use them on your sales call, Recognizing these words is not the same as using them, Everyone can name “objection handling.”, Almost nobody can sit in silence after \"I need to think about it.\", Sales IQ isn’t vocabulary., It’s what you do in the 3 seconds after the prospect hesitates., Which one do you skip? That’s usually the leak., Make a note of this post.]",
